					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-30 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><div style="text-align: center"><img src="http://i41.photobucket.com/albums/e256/knitla/blue-scholars-tour.jpg" alt="" width="400" height="562" /></div><br /><br /><div align="center"><strong>TONIGHT! </strong><strong>TONIGHT! </strong><strong>TONIGHT! </strong><strong>TONIGHT! </strong><strong>TONIGHT!<br /><br />LET THE ENTIRE MASSLINE CREW KNOW HOW LA GETS DOWN. Ceeeeeee - AAAAAA =)<br /><br /></strong><div align="left"><br />Enjoy the 206 weather while it lasts, suckas!<br />Peace<br />daps1<br /></div></div><strong><br /><br /></strong><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-30 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><strong>Good news and UPDATES (from DM):<br /><br />Blue Scholars</strong> return from blasting the West Coast on the <strong>MassLine tour </strong>to celebrate the release of their highly anticipated new album <em><strong>&quot;Bayani&quot;</strong></em> in Seattle and Portland with a series of free in-store performances. <br /><br /><ul><li>June 11th Queen Anne East Street 11pm (album goes on sale at Midnight) </li></ul><ul><li>June 12th Northgate Silver Platters 6pm </li></ul><ul><li>June 13th Southcenter Silver Platters 6pm </li></ul><ul><li>June 14th Portland Music Millenium 6pm </li></ul><ul><li>June 16th Crossroads Mall Silver Platters in the Mall 2pm</li></ul><br />All performances are <strong>FREE</strong> and <strong>ALL AGES</strong> and <strong>Geo</strong> and <strong>Sabzi</strong> will be signing CD&#39;s after they perform new songs from the new album. You can also pick up their new merch and get <strong>Bayani</strong> at special sale prices.<br /><br /> <em>&quot;...easily one of the most poignant, important, and best albums ever to come from the Northwest.&quot;</em> - ThreeImaginaryGirls.com<br /><br />These are the only Seattle shows for <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> until <strong>July 27 at The Capitol Hill Block Party</strong>. Come celebrate the release of <strong>Bayani</strong> and support the NW hip hop revolution!<br /><br />Also check out <strong>Blue Scholars live on KEXP 90.3 FM Tuesday June 12 at 9:30 am</strong> premiering tracks from <strong>Bayani</strong> and discussing the new album, life and whatever else comes up. (online at <a href="http://www.kexp.org/" target="_blank">www.kexp.org</a>)<br /><br /><hr /><br />Bring &#39;em back home!<br />Peace<br />daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-29 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/193/519429529_33789c3216.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="425" /><br />RA holdin it down at the 2007 Sasquatch Music Festival. Pic courtesy of M.<br /><br /><hr />A message from Gabe Teodros regarding Sasquatch 07:<br /><br />&quot;<em>we went on mad early on saturday (1pm or so) on the yeti stage... it
was my first time at the gorge and the beauty of our surroundings just
took my breath away... it felt great being backstage like 20 deep... it
was like we brought a whole neighborhood, the way it should be.&nbsp; the
set ended up being my favorite show we&#39;ve ever put on... better then
the release party... we had the full band... amos miller on keys, mark
oi on guitar, aaron walker-loud on drums, camilo estrada on bass, and
wd4d on cuts... and helping out on vocals was jerm from alpha-p (do u),
sistahailstorm &amp; ispire from canary sing (warriors rrreeemix),
kwame (no label), and rufio (rest o&#39; me dayz)... as well as nin-g the
hyphogropher dancing along with hailstorm, rufio, etc... if you missed
it, damn ya&#39;ll missed a show!!!&nbsp; ozomatli killed it as well... i&#39;m sad
we missed bjork... but the land and the sky definitley outshined
everyone (it was so beautiful)&nbsp; to everyone that came throo... thanks!&nbsp;
we&#39;re in phoenix now... hella homesick and i can&#39;t wait to see ya&#39;ll
mothertruckers again...</em>&quot;<br /><br />southendfalife<br />-- teodros<br /><hr /><br />More reviews, photos and video from this weekend <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=2372.0" target="_blank">HERE</a>!<br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-24 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://i8.tinypic.com/664ac6g.jpg" alt="" /><br />
Massline artists rock what looks like a pretty intimate, in-your-face
setting at Spokane&#39;s Raw Sushi on 5/18/07. Photo courtesy Luis Sanchez.
<br />
<br />
Big ups to Blake Lewis on his successful American Idol run. And big up to flashforwards on ABC&#39;s &quot;Lost&quot;!<br />
<br />
Peace<br />
daps1<br />
<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-23 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://a67.ac-images.myspacecdn.com/images01/27/l_9c6e3b34ed42d749702ab1959ad842ea.jpg" alt="" width="360" height="270" /><br /><strong><em>What it do Salt Lake City?!?!</em></strong><br /><br />More pics of ML artists in SLC <a href="http://www.myspace.com/133454953" target="_blank"><strong>here</strong></a>. Props to Rawsheed Jenkins for the link. If any of y&#39;all got pics for us from this current tour, <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=1845.0">holler at this post</a> and i&#39;ll put the best ones up!<br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=14